e-curvine-image-for-fluid","content":"For a shared cluster, tag and push it to a registry, then update the image in the Fluid manifests:","locale":"en"},"56":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration-54","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration#build-the-curvine-image-for-fluid","content":"Set the same image in `CacheRuntimeClass` and `ThinRuntimeProfile`.","locale":"en"},"57":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration-55","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration#build-the-curvine-image-for-fluid","content":"The CacheRuntime `DataLoad` path has been verified with Fluid chart `helm-chart-fluid-1.1.0-alpha.10`, whose Fluid image tag is `v1.1.0-676f47a`. Older or custom Fluid charts may need the fallback notes in the DataLoad section.","locale":"en"},"58":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration-56","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration#cacheruntime-quick-start","content":"Use CacheRuntime when Fluid should create and manage the Curvine cache pods.","locale":"en"},"59":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration-57","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration#1-create-the-cacheruntimeclass","content":"Start from:","locale":"en"},"60":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration-58","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration#1-create-the-cacheruntimeclass","content":"Apply it:","locale":"en"},"61":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration-59","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration#1-create-the-cacheruntimeclass","content":"The class describes how Fluid starts each Curvine role:","locale":"en"},"62":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration-60","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration#1-create-the-cacheruntimeclass","content":"| Role     | Kubernetes workload | Responsibility                        |\n| -------- | ------------------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| `master` | `StatefulSet`       | Curvine metadata and journal service. |","locale":"en","table":"table-2"},"63":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration-61","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration#1-create-the-cacheruntimeclass","content":"| Role     | Kubernetes workload | Responsibility |\n| -------- | ------------------- | -------------- |\n| `worker` | `StatefulSet`       | Cache storage. |","locale":"en","table":"table-2"},"64":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration-62","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration#1-create-the-cacheruntimeclass","content":"| Role     | Kubernetes workload | Responsibility                   |\n| -------- | ------------------- | -------------------------------- |\n| `client` | `DaemonSet`         | FUSE mount for application pods. |","locale":"en","table":"table-2"},"65":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration-63","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration#1-create-the-cacheruntimeclass","content":"The class also defines `executionEntries.mountUFS`. Fluid calls this entry so Curvine can mount Dataset UFS paths before serving the Dataset. In the Curvine image, the script is:","locale":"en"},"66":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration-64","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration#1-create-the-cacheruntimeclass","content":"The script reads `FLUID_RUNTIME_CONFIG_PATH`, runs `cv mount` f