orage Configuration","locale":"en"},"266":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration-12","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration#oss-configuration","content":"OSS Configuration","locale":"en"},"267":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration-13","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration#hdfs-configuration","content":"HDFS Configuration","locale":"en"},"268":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration-14","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration#hdfs-environment-requirements","content":"HDFS Environment Requirements","locale":"en"},"269":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration-15","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration#compilation-requirements","content":"Compilation Requirements","locale":"en"},"270":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration-16","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration#runtime-environment-requirements","content":"Runtime Environment Requirements","locale":"en"},"271":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration-17","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration#overview","content":"Curvine integrates with OpenDAL (Open Data Access Layer) at its core, providing powerful storage ecosystem support. This integration enables Curvine to work seamlessly with various storage backends while maintaining a unified interface.","locale":"en"},"272":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration-18","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration#what-is-opendal","content":"OpenDAL is a data access layer that provides unified APIs to access various storage services. It serves as an abstraction layer between applications and storage systems, offering:","locale":"en"},"273":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration-19","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration#what-is-opendal","content":"**Unified Interface**: Consistent APIs across different storage backends","locale":"en"},"274":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration-20","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration#what-is-opendal","content":"**Multi-Storage Support**: Support for object storage, filesystems, databases, and more","locale":"en"},"275":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration-21","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration#what-is-opendal","content":"**High Performance**: Optimized data access paths and caching mechanisms","locale":"en"},"276":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration-22","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration#what-is-opendal","content":"**Extensibility**: Easy addition of new storage backend support","locale":"en"},"277":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration-23","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration#what-is-opendal","content":"**Reliability**: Built-in retry mechanisms and error handling","locale":"en"},"278":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration-24","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration#supported-storage-backends","content":"Through OpenDAL integration, Curvine currently supports the following storage services:","locale":"en"},"279":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration-25","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration#object-storage","content":"**Amazon S3**: AWS object storage service, supports `s3://` and `s3a://` protocols","locale":"en"},"280":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration-26","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration#object-storage","content":"**Alibaba Cloud OSS**: Alibaba Cloud object storage service, supports `oss://` protocol","locale":"en"},"281":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration-27","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration#object-storage","content":"**Tencent Cloud COS**: Tencent Cloud object storage, supports `cos://` protocol","locale":"en"},"282":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration-28","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration#object-storage","content":"**Azure Blob Storage**: Microsoft Azure object storage, supports `azblob://` protocol","locale":"en"},"283":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration-29","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration#object-storage","content":"**Google Cloud Storage**: Google cloud storage, supports `gcs://` and `gs://` protocols","locale":"en"},"284":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration-30","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration#distributed-file-systems","content":"**HDFS**: Hadoop Distributed File System, supports `hdfs://` protocol (requires special environment setup)","locale":"en"},"285":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration-31","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration#core-features","content":"Through OpenDAL integration, Curvine provides two core features for accessing external storage:","locale":"en"},"286":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration-32","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration#mount-feature---mounting-external-storage","content":"The `mount` feature allows mounting external storage systems into Curvine's namespace, making external storage appear as part of the Curvine filesystem.","locale":"en"},"287":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration-33","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration#load-feature---loading-external-data","content":"Mount an external path once, including its UFS credentials and endpoint, then\nload through the mounted Curvine path. This keeps credentials out of every\nLoad invocation and makes the source-to-target mapping unambiguous.","locale":"en"},"288":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration-34","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration#load-feature---loading-external-data","content":"When Transfer is enabled in the client configuration, the same `cv load`\ncommand submits an independent Transfer job. See\nTransfer Service deployment\nfor service and client configuration.","locale":"en"},"289":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration-35","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration#s3-compatible-storage-configuration","content":"| Parameter         | Description         | Example                   |\n| ----------------- | ------------------- | ------------------------- |\n| `s3.endpoint_url` | S3 service endpoint | `http://s3.amazonaws.com` |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"290":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration-36","page_id":"/docs/Architecture