d":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/k8s-Deployment-119","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/k8s-Deployment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/k8s-Deployment#worker","content":"| Parameter             | Default | Description   |\n| --------------------- | ------- | ------------- |\n| `worker.nodeSelector` | `{}`    | Node selector |","locale":"en","table":"table-7"},"1458":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/k8s-Deployment-120","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/k8s-Deployment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/k8s-Deployment#worker","content":"| Parameter            | Default | Description |\n| -------------------- | ------- | ----------- |\n| `worker.tolerations` | `[]`    | Tolerations |","locale":"en","table":"table-7"},"1459":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/k8s-Deployment-121","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/k8s-Deployment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/k8s-Deployment#worker","content":"| Parameter         | Default | Description    |\n| ----------------- | ------- | -------------- |\n| `worker.affinity` | `{}`    | Affinity rules |","locale":"en","table":"table-7"},"1460":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/k8s-Deployment-122","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/k8s-Deployment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/k8s-Deployment#worker","content":"The chart keeps two master web ports: `master.webPort` (`9000`, the admin\nconsole, written to `[web].port`) and `master.web1Port` (`9001`, the master\nmetrics listener, written to `[master].web_port`). Standalone code defaults\ndiffer — admin console `9000`, master metrics `9010`, Worker `9002` — so always\nread the effective ports from the generated ConfigMap rather than assuming.","locale":"en"},"1461":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/k8s-Deployment-123","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/k8s-Deployment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/k8s-Deployment#worker","content":"`worker.s3Gateway.*` is live: with `enabled: true` the chart adds the\n`[s3_gateway]` block and `worker.enable_s3_gateway` to the ConfigMap, and creates\na Service on `worker.s3Gateway.listen` (default `0.0.0.0:9900`). The worker\ncontainer still only runs `/entrypoint.sh worker start`, so nothing starts the\ngateway binary for you — run `curvine-s3-gateway` as a sidecar or a separate\nDeployment until the chart ships one.","locale":"en"},"1462":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/k8s-Deployment-124","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/k8s-Deployment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/k8s-Deployment#transfer","content":"| Parameter          | Default | Description                                                                                      |\n| ------------------ | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `transfer.enabled` | `false` | Creates no Transfer resources until enabled; disabled mode preserves the legacy Master Load API. |","locale":"en","table":"table-8"},"1463":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/k8s-Deployment-125","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/k8s-Deployment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/k8s-Deployment#transfer","content":"| Parameter           | Default | Description                                                                                                            |\n| ------------------