46":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-30","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#native-cli-cv","content":"Get a quick overview:","locale":"en"},"2947":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-31","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#native-cli-cv","content":"The current top-level commands in source are:","locale":"en"},"2948":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-32","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#native-cli-cv","content":"`load-status`, `cancel-load`, `transfer-status`, and `cancel-transfer` are still accepted but hidden from `--help`; they remain as compatibility shortcuts for the legacy job API.","locale":"en"},"2949":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-33","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#native-cli-cv","content":"All `cv` commands accept these global options:","locale":"en"},"2950":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-34","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#native-cli-cv","content":"| Global option   | Description                                                                                                                       |\n| --------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--conf <PATH>` | Override the cluster config file for this invocation. If omitted, the CLI uses its normal configured path or `CURVINE_CONF_FILE`. |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"2951":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-35","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#native-cli-cv","content":"| Global option    