uild-cached`，结果在 `build/dist`。）"],[425,"[[1]] 10.39M Storage I/O Per Second From One Thread"],[4025,"[[1]] 10.39M Storage I/O Per Second From One Thread"],[3276,"**`blocked_versions`:** release versions listed here are **always rejected**\nregardless of the mode. This is an emergency backstop for known-bad builds\n(see the known-incompatible list on the release notes page)."],[6881,"**`blocked_versions`：** 列出的版本无论模式如何都**总是被拒绝**。这是针对已知问题版本的紧急兜底手段（见发布说明页的已知不兼容清单）。"],[348,"**`curvine_*` C helper functions**: Small C wrappers that set struct fields at known offsets. For example, Rust calls `curvine_spdk_async_ctx_init(...)` rather than manipulating C struct fields directly. At init, a runtime `sizeof()` check compares the Rust buffer size against the real C struct size, catching ABI drift immediately."],[3948,"**`curvine_*` C 辅助函数**：用小型 C wrapper 在已知偏移处设置结构体字段。例如 Rust 调用 `curvine_spdk_async_ctx_init(...)`，而不是直接操作 C 结构体字段。初始化时会通过运行时 `sizeof()` 检查比较 Rust 缓冲区大小和真实 C 结构体大小，一旦 ABI 漂移就能立即发现。"],[2331,"**`CurvineClient`** — native bindings, explicit config, chunks you control:"],[5939,"**`CurvineClient`**——原生绑定，配置显式、chunk 大小可控："],[2332,"**`CurvineFileSystem`** — an fsspec implementation, registered as the\n`curvinefs` spec, so pandas, dask, and anything fsspec-aware can read the\ncluster directly:"],[5940,"**`CurvineFileSystem`**——fsspec 实现，注册为 `curvinefs` spec，因此 pandas、dask 等支持 fsspec 的库可以直接读取集群："],[3274,"**`mode = \"diagnose\"` (default):** incompatible peers are allowed, and the\nmaster logs a warning describing the peer, its version, and the expected\nbound. This is the safe default and never breaks an existing mixed-version\ncluster."],[6879,"**`mode = \"diagnose\"`（默认）：** 不兼容的 peer 被允许，master 记录告警，内容包括 peer、其版本和期望的边界。这是安全默认值，不会破坏已有的混合版本集群。"],[3275,"**`mode = \"enforce\"`:** incompatible peers are rejected with an explicit\nerror that includes the actual peer version and the upgrade suggestion."],[6880,"**`mode = \"enforce\"`：** 不兼容的 peer 被拒绝，错误信息包含实际 peer 版本和升级建议。"],[3229,"**0.3.x legacy workers / clients with 0.4.x master.** Workers and clients\nrunning 0.3.x (or earlier) do not send structured `component_info`. The master\ndetects them as legacy peers: allowed with a warning in `diagnose` mode\n(default), rejected only in `enforce` mode. No data loss or protocol error\noccurs; the master simply cannot verify their protocol version, release\nversion, or capabilities."],[6834,"**0.3.x 旧版 worker / client 对接 0.4.x master。** 运行 0.3.x（或更早）的 worker 和 client 不上报结构化 `component_info`。master 将其识别为旧版 peer：`diagnose` 模式（默认）下允许并告警，仅在 `enforce` 模式下拒绝。不会发生数据丢失或协议错误，master 只是无法校验它们的协议版本、发布版本或能力。"],[2033,"**1. Metadata operation performance**"],[5639,"**1. 元数据操作性能**"],[2057,"**2. Data Read/Write Performance**"],[5663,"**2. 数据读写性能**"],[2116,"**3. Resource consumption**"],[5722,"**3. 资源消耗情况**"],[3034,"**About `--provider`**: some URI schemes can map to multiple implementations. For example, `oss://...` may be handled either by OSS-HDFS / JindoSDK or by OpenDAL, so `--provider` lets you force the implementation."],[372,"**Acquire**: Pop a cached qpair (zero FFI). If pool is empty, call `curvine_spdk_alloc_io_qpair` to allocate a new one."],[3972,"**Acquire**：弹出一个缓存 qpair（零 FFI）。如果池为空，则调用 `curvine_spdk_alloc_io_qpair` 分配新 qpair。"],[3338,"**Active Worker Count**: Real-time display of currently online Worker nodes"],[352,"**Active**: Drains the incoming request channel, submits NVMe commands via `spdk_nvme_ns_cmd_read`/`write`, polls qpairs for completions, and invokes per-I/O callbacks. When the queue is empty, it spins for `spin_iter` iterations before transitioning to Idle. This **spin-before-park** avoids an `eventfd` wake round-trip when the next I/O arrives immediately, keeping the poller in a low-overhead polling loop instead of a syscall-heavy park/unpark cycle."],[3952,"**Active**：从请求 channel 中取出待处理请求，通过 `spdk_nvme_ns_cmd_read`/`write` 提交 NVMe 命令，轮询 qpair 完成队列，并调用每个 I/O 的回调。队列为空后，它会先自旋 `spin_iter` 次再切回 Idle。这种 **spin-before-park** 策略避免了下一个 I/O 紧接到来时产生一次 `eventfd` 唤醒往返，使 poller 保持在低开销轮询循环中，而不是频繁执行 park/unpark 系统调用。"],[280,"**Alibaba Cloud OSS**: Alibaba Cloud object storage service, supports `oss://` protocol"],[194,"**Allocate blocks**: The client requests new blocks from the Master. The Master chooses Worker(s) (and replicas if needed), records block allocations in the journal (e.g. `AddBlock`, `CompleteFile`), and returns block locations to the client."],[413,"**Allocator improvements**: Enhance performance, reduce fragmentation, contention, and time complexity under high workload."],[3487,"**Always use FUSE3** in production — FUSE2 delivers only ~50% of FUSE3 throughput."],[7092,"**Always use FUSE3** in production — FUSE2 delivers only ~50% of FUSE3 throughput."],[279,"**Amazon S3**: AWS object storage service, supports `s3://` and `s3a://` protocols"],[3879,"**Amazon S3**：AWS 的对象存储服务，支持 `s3://` 和 `s3a://` 协议"],[2028,"**Analytical Databases and OLAP Engines**: Provides high-speed caching for analytical databases and OLAP engines, significantly improving complex query performance and reducing data analysis time"],[1728,"**Application Layer**: Includes curvine-fuse, applications accessed via SDK, CLI management tools, etc. For details, refer to Access Methods."],[898,"**Approve deliberately.** Drafts exist for a reason. Check the issue, PR body, or review comment before saying yes."],[245,"**Asynchronous data copy**: the actual data blocks of files are asynchronously copied from Curvine to UFS in the background. The copy process does not affect local metadata read/write operations and avoids slowing down write speed. If UFS is temporarily unavailable, the copy task automatically retries until synchronization succeeds."],[2000,"**Asynchronous I/O**: Asynchronous I/O design fully utilizes system resources, avoiding blocking waits and improving system concurrent processing capabilities"],[199,"**AsyncThrough** (default): Data is written to Curvine first (return immediately), then asynchronously synced to UFS."],[3799,"**AsyncThrough**（默认）：先写 Curvine 后立即返回，再异步同步到 UFS。"],[2004,"**Automatic Failover**: Automatic failover mechanism that switches to backup nodes when primary nodes fail, ensuring system high availability"],[3363,"**Available Capacity Display**: Shows the currently available storage capacity"],[3343,"**Available Storage Space**: Shows remaining available storage space"],[282,"**Azure Blob Storage**: Microsoft Azure object storage, supports `azblob://` protocol"],[3882,"**Azure Blob Storage**：Microsoft Azure 的对象存储，支持 `azblob://` 协议"],[2029,"**Big Data Computing**: Provides high-speed caching for big data computing scenarios, reducing data read/write time"],[388,"**Block alignment**: All offsets are aligned down to the device block size. This is required by the NVMe specification — unaligned DMA addresses cause controller errors."],[1961,"**BlockClient Pool**: Manages block_reader / block_writer for local and remote access"],[5568,"**BlockClient Pool**：管理本地和远程访问的 block_reader / block_writer"],[1976,"**BlockStore**: Manages block lifecycle and local storage"],[5583,"**BlockStore**：管理块生命周期和本地存储"],[873,"**Body:** Summary, Issue Describe / Design, Changes, Test verified, and Dependencies"],[3352,"**Breadcrumb Navigation**: Shows the complete directory hierarchy structure"],[1522,"**Building:** `make build` / `make all` — Build; output in `build/dist`. `make dist` — Build and create tar.gz in project root. `make dist-only` — Package existing `build/dist` only."],[2023,"**Built-in observability**: Exposes monitoring and metrics for cluster components"],[192,"**Cache hit**: If the path is under a Curvine-native file (not a UFS mount), data is read from Workers as above. For paths under a **UFS mount**, the unified file system and cache behavior apply: the client may serve from Curvine cache when valid, or from UFS on cache miss (with optional automatic caching when TTL is set)."],[197,"**Cache**: Data is written only to Curvine (Workers); not written to UFS."],[3797,"**Cache**：仅写入 Curvine（Worker），不写 UFS。"],[200,"**CacheThrough**: Data is written synchronously to both Curvine and UFS before returning."],[3800,"**CacheThrough**：同步写入 Curvine 与 UFS 后返回。"],[3364,"**Capacity Statistics**: Real-time updated capacity usage information"],[3344,"**Capacity Utilization**: Displays storage usage rate through progress bars and percentages"],[900,"**CI is the referee.** Formatting, compilation, tests, and the PR title check still decide whether a change can land. Skills do not bypass them."],[4499,"**CI 说了算。** 格式化、编译、测试和 PR 标题检查仍然决定一个改动能否合入，skill 不会绕过它们。"],[386,"**Cleanup on close**: Buffers are freed via `curvine_spdk_dma_free` in `SpdkBdev::drop`. If inflight I/Os do not drain before the drop deadline, the buffer pointers are nulled to prevent use-after-free (safe leak)."],[1957,"**CLI (`cv`)**: Admin tools for fs ops, report, and cluster management"],[5564,"**CLI (`cv`)**：文件系统操作、报告和集群管理的管理工具"],[1744,"**Client Library**: Provides multi-language APIs, communicating with Master and Worker nodes via RPC"],[2017,"**Cloud-native integration**: Supports CSI-based deployment and Kubernetes-oriented packaging workflows"],[3402,"**Cluster Comparison**: Compare configuration differences between different environments"],[912,"**Cluster core (required):** Start `curvine-master` and `curvine-worker` on the intended hosts. The cluster is operational once Master and Workers are running; you can use the CLI (`cv`) or SDK without FUSE."],[3334,"**Cluster Status**: Displays whether the cluster is currently active, including uptime information"],[3387,"**cluster_id**: Unique identifier for the cluster"],[6992,"**cluster_id**：集群的唯一标识符"],[226,"**Collaboration logic**: adopts an on-demand loading and divided-response approach. For example, when a user lists the contents of a directory, the in-memory directory tree first quickly returns the names of all files and folders in the directory to ensure response speed. When the user needs to view detailed information about a file, such as size and modification time, the system then performs a batch query in RocksDB for the corresponding detailed information and returns it all at once. This ensures speed without wasting memory resources."],[2944,"**Compatibility wrapper `dfs`**: bundled in the distribution; `fs` / `report` go through Java `CurvineShell` and keep Hadoop `FsShell` style."],[175,"**Components**: `MasterHandler` serves RPC; `MasterFilesystem` and `FsDir` hold the directory/file and block mapping; `JournalWriter` writes entries; `WorkerManager` tracks Workers and block placement; `MountManager` manages UFS mount points."],[2335,"**Config file**: Most SDKs accept a config file path (e.g. `conf/curvine-cluster.toml`). The same file is used by the CLI (`cv`) and FUSE."],[2145,"**Configuration**: The node where FUSE runs must have access to the cluster config (e.g. `conf/curvine-cluster.toml`) and correct Master address."],[2953,"**Conventions:**"],[233,"**Core advantage**: write speed is greatly improved. There is no need to wait for the log to be synchronized to most machines before completing the local modification. Local write latency can be reduced to a few milliseconds. In high-concurrency scenarios, such as creating a large number of small files, throughput can increase several times, perfectly adapting to high-frequency small-operation scenarios."],[232,"**Core process**: the Leader node first updates its own in-memory directory tree, then writes to the local RocksDB to complete the local data modification, and then synchronizes the log of this modification to other Follower nodes in the cluster to complete consistency synchronization."],[2124,"**crates/client**: Rust client core, unified filesystem, transfer job client, and benchmark runner"],[5730,"**crates/client**：Rust 客户端核心、统一文件系统、传输作业客户端与压测运行器"],[2120,"**crates/common**: Shared configuration, protocol, metadata, filesystem, storage, and UFS APIs"],[5726,"**crates/common**：共享配置、协议、元数据、文件系统、存储与 UFS API"],[2119,"**crates/core**: Runtime, RPC, networking, I/O, allocation, metrics, and fault-injection primitives"],[5725,"**crates/core**：运行时、RPC、网络、I/O、内存分配、指标与故障注入基础能力"],[2121,"**crates/metadata**: Raft-based metadata replication"],[5727,"**crates/metadata**：基于 Raft 的元数据复制"],[2123,"**crates/server**: Standalone Transfer service for Load and Export jobs"],[5729,"**crates/server**：独立处理 Load / Export 作业的 Transfer 服务"],[2274,"**Credential store path:**"],[1956,"**CSI Driver**: Kubernetes volume driver (curvine-csi)"],[5563,"**CSI 驱动**：Kubernetes 卷驱动 (curvine-csi)"],[1525,"**CSI:** `make curvine-csi` — Build curvine-csi Docker image."],[5123,"**CSI**：`make curvine-csi` — 构建 curvine-csi 镜像"],[1953,"**Curvine Client**: Data read/write operations are implemented by the client, which calls Curvine server-side interfaces through RPC (metadata from Master, block data from Workers). The client supports multiple access methods:"],[1729,"**Curvine Cluster Service Layer**: Consists of **curvine-master** (can be multiple nodes for HA, forming a Raft group) and **curvine-worker** nodes forming the Curvine cluster."],[2144,"**Curvine cluster** is running (Master and Worker started). See Bare Metal Deployment or Quick Start."],[5560,"**Curvine 客户端**：数据读写操作由客户端实现，通过 RPC 调用 Curvine 服务器端接口（从 Master 获取元数据，从 Worker 获取块数据）。客户端支持多种访问方式："],[5750,"**Curvine 集群**已启动（已启动 Master 与 Worker）。参见 裸机部署 或 快速开始。"],[5336,"**Curvine 集群服务层**：由 **curvine-master**（可多节点部署形成 Raft 组，实现高可用）与 **curvine-worker** 节点共同组成 Curvine 集群。"],[2128,"**curvine-cli**: Native CLI (`cv`) for cluster, mount, fs, and load operations"],[5734,"**curvine-cli**：原生命令行工具 `cv`"],[2130,"**curvine-csi**: CSI driver for Kubernetes storage integration"],[5736,"**curvine-csi**：面向 Kubernetes 的 CSI 驱动"],[2125,"**curvine-fuse**: FUSE daemon for POSIX-style access"],[5731,"**curvine-fuse**：提供 POSIX 访问的 FUSE 守护进程"],[2126,"**curvine-libsdk**: Java and Python SDK bindings built on top of the native client"],[5732,"**curvine-libsdk**：基于原生客户端封装的 Java / Python 