rallelism and locality |"],[3514,"| Data Pattern           | Recommended Block Size | Rationale                                 |\n| ---------------------- | ---------------------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| Large sequential files | 1GB                    | Reduces connection count for random reads |"],[7119,"| Data Pattern           | Recommended Block Size | Rationale                                 |\n| ---------------------- | ---------------------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| Large sequential files | 1GB                    | Reduces connection count for random reads |"],[3515,"| Data Pattern           | Recommended Block Size | Rationale                         |\n| ---------------------- | ---------------------- | --------------------------------- |\n| Video / model binaries | 256MB - 1GB            | High throughput sequential access |"],[7120,"| Data Pattern           | Recommended Block Size | Rationale                         |\n| ---------------------- | ---------------------- | --------------------------------- |\n| Video / model binaries | 256MB - 1GB            | High throughput sequential access |"],[3512,"| Data Pattern        | Recommended Block Size | Rationale                                     |\n| ------------------- | ---------------------- | --------------------------------------------- |\n| Small files (< 4MB) | 4MB                    | One block per file, minimal metadata overhead |"],[7117,"| Data Pattern        | Recommended Block Size | Rationale                                     |\n| ------------------- | ---------------------- | --------------------------------------------- |\n| Small files (< 4MB) | 4MB                    | One block per file, minimal metadata overhead |"],[3483,"| Data Temperature         | Storage Tier | TTL | Replicas | Example                   |\n| ------------------------ | ------------ | --- | -------- | ------------------------- |\n| Cold (infrequent access) | HDD          | 30d | 1        | Archives, historical logs |"],[7088,"| Data Temperature         | Storage Tier | TTL | Replicas | Example                   |\n| ------------------------ | ------------ | --- | -------- | ------------------------- |\n| Cold (infrequent access) | HDD          | 30d | 1        | Archives, historical logs |"],[3482,"| Data Temperature      | Storage Tier | TTL | Replicas | Example                          |\n| --------------------- | ------------ | --- | -------- | -------------------------------- |\n| Warm (regular access) | SSD          | 7d  | 2        | Training datasets, Parquet files |"],[7087,"| Data Temperature      | Storage Tier | TTL | Replicas | Example                          |\n| --------------------- | ------------ | --- | -------- | -------------------------------- |\n| Warm (regular access) | SSD          | 7d  | 2        | Training datasets, Parquet files |"],[3481,"| Data Temperature      | Storage Tier | TTL | Replicas | Example                       |\n| --------------------- | ------------ | --- | -------- | ----------------------------- |\n| Hot (frequent access) | MEM          | 1d  | 2-3      | Model weights, feature tables |"],[7086,"| Data Temperature      | Storage Tier | TTL | Replicas | Example                       |\n| --------------------- | ------------ | --- | -------- | ----------------------------- |\n| Hot (frequent access) | MEM          | 1d  | 2-3      | Model weights, feature tables |"],[2690,"| Dimension           | Curvine Key Point                                                                              |\n| ------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Product positioning | Distributed file cache with POSIX mounting, with a user experience equivalent to a local disk. |"],[2694,"| Dimension          | Curvine Key Point                                                                                                          |\n| ------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Storage management | Multi-media tiered storage. The client can specify priority, and data falls back automatically when space is insufficient. |"],[2693,"| Dimension         | Curvine Key Point                                                                                                 |\n| ----------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Advanced features | Supports extended attributes, symbolic and hard links, timeout-based file locks, sparse files, and preallocation. |"],[2692,"| Dimension        | Curvine Key Point                                                           |\n| ---------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Write capability | Supports random writes and multi-client concurrent writes to the same file. |"],[2695,"| Dimension        | Curvine Key Point                                              |\n| ---------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Space management | `mtime`-based TTL expiration plus optional quota LRU eviction. |"],[2691,"| Dimension       | Curvine Key Point                                                                                        |\n| --------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Core advantages | Unified namespace, intelligent tiered storage, TTL + LRU space management, and complete POSIX semantics. |"],[2641,"| Feature                             | Description                                                                                                                                                                           |\n| ----------------------------------- | ----------------------------